---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="404: Page Not Found">
  <main class="prose mx-auto px-4 py-16 text-center">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold mb-4">404</h1>
    <p class="text-xl mb-8">Sorry, the page you’re looking for doesn’t exist.</p>
    <div class="mb-8">
      <strong>Your implementation plan is comprehensive and aligns with best practices for a modular, maintainable Astro site.</strong>
      <br />
      Here’s a focused checklist to ensure your existing content is visible and your site is fully functional:
      <ul class="text-left inline-block mt-4">
        <li>✔️ Content files exist in <code>src/content/blog/</code> and <code>src/content/projects/</code></li>
        <li>✔️ Content indexing and JSON generation is working</li>
        <li>✔️ Dynamic routing and templates are set up</li>
        <li>✔️ Navigation links to all main sections</li>
        <li>✔️ <code>astro.config.mjs</code> base path is correct</li>
        <li>✔️ Build and serve steps complete without errors</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Go Home</a>
  </main>
</Layout>
